    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Select the function that is continuous at $x=2.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The correct answer is shown below. Despite the fact that the function has a discontinuity at $x=5$, the graph can be drawn in the neighborhood of $x=2$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186068695/plots/0d17acb79f4af1bf11afeaff7eb51382c0eebb69539f507e807b988b2571c19d.png)\n\nAll the other given graphs contain breaks at $x=2$ and it would be impossible to draw them in the neighborhood of $x=2$ without taking the pencil off of the paper.",
