      ":question/problem": "Select the function that is continuous at $x=0.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The correct answer is shown below.  Indeed, despite the fact that the function has a discontinuity at $x=4$, the graph can be drawn in a neighborhood of $x=0$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186068695/plots/d64ca3f3e7de5908a8aff5b5214fa2419329c745b7f614c208a3daf6cc4f7066.png)\n\n   \n\nAll the other given graphs contain breaks at $x=0$ and it would be impossible to draw them in a neighborhood of $x=0$ without taking the pencil off of the paper.",
