      "title": "Determining Whether a Function Is Continuous at a Given Point"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Select the function that is continuous at $x=-4.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The correct answer is shown below. Despite the fact that the function has a discontinuity at $x=2$, the graph can be drawn in the neighborhood of $x=-4$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186068695/plots/fc1b34437f339c587ea17c2b59399be6bfe28d53a27564a41d8ee6bd6bc714e6.png)\n\nAll the other given graphs contain breaks at $x=-4$ and it would be impossible to draw them in the neighborhood of $x=-4$ without taking the pencil off of the paper.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
