    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Select the function that is continuous at $x=-7.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The correct answer is shown below. Despite the fact that the function has a discontinuity at $x=-1$, the graph can be drawn in the neighborhood of $x=-7$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186068695/plots/2bb7e3e212914e08469b2960602ed1a70c5d9e23f9fe2ef018063d4663ab315c.png)\n\nAll the other given graphs contain breaks at $x=-7$ and it would be impossible to draw them in the neighborhood of $x=-7$ without taking the pencil off of the paper.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
