      ":question/problem": "Select the function that is continuous at $x=-4.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The correct answer is shown below. Despite the fact that the function has a discontinuity at $x=-1$, the graph can be drawn in the neighborhood of $x=-4$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186068695/plots/b20e969a1af4d041cc6c84cba075a63b91a17af09733439b856fb6ecad3561bc.png)\n\nAll the other given graphs contain breaks at $x=-4$ and it would be impossible to draw them in the neighborhood of $x=-4$ without taking the pencil off of the paper.",
