      "title": "Determining Whether a Function Is Continuous at a Given Point"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Select the function that is continuous at $x=1.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Of the given options, the only one where we can draw the graph of the function without taking our pencil off of the paper in a neighborhood of $x=1$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186068695/plots/bf01d0cf2acbc4297d3e90c171769de0663aef9fe3d01bd7b7157079898a83fa.png)\n\nAll other given options have breaks or asymptotes at $x=1$, so it is impossible to draw the function in the neighborhood of $x=1$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
